    "result_text": "All green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: when a computed `customerCode` collides with an existing owner's, append `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\nI added one small, cohesive function and wired it into the POST-owners pipeline \u2014 deliberately keeping structural impact low:\n\n- **New `DeduplicateCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 a single-method function class (`WMC_other = 0`, low CC) that reads the code assigned by `AssignCustomerCode`, collects existing owners' codes via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique. It runs after Assign and before Save, so the persisted code is already de-duplicated.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `deduplicateCode` step between `assignCode` and `countNamesakes`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nI did **not** touch `AssignCustomerCode` or any other existing function, so no existing method's complexity or surrounding-class WMC was paid for \u2014 the change is a new unit plus one YAML edit (2 files). `AcceptanceTest` and the full build pass green.",
